gy systems; reticle inspection and metrology systems; wafer inspection and metrology systems; semiconductor software solutions; KLA Pro systems; and specialty semiconductor manufacturing, benchtop metrology, surface characterization, material strength characterization, and electrical property measurement products. It also provides etch, plasma dicing, deposition and other wafer processing technologies and solutions; direct imaging, inspection, optical shaping, inkjet, and additive printing, as well as computer-aided manufacturing and engineering solutions; and components. In addition, the company offers service programs. It serves semiconductor, and semiconductor-related and electronic device manufacturers. The company operates in China, Taiwan, Korea, North America, Japan, Europe, Israel, and rest of Asia. The company was formerly known as KLA-Tencor Corporation and changed its name to KLA Corporation in July 2019. KLA Corporation was incorporated in 1975 and is headquartered in Milpitas, California.","employees":17000,"website":"https://www.kla.com","country":"United States","city":"Milpitas","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Richard P. Wallace","title":"President, CEO & Executive Director"},{"name":"Mr. Bren D. Higgins","title":"Executive VP & CFO"},{"name":"Ms. Mary Beth Wilkinson","title":"Executive VP, Chief Legal Officer & Corporate Secretary"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":17.74,"tpe":28.93,"ps":5.856,"pfcf":31.1,"peg":0.925,"pb":7.897,"ev_ebitda":19.28,"rev_growth":0.205,"eps_growth":0.5,"eps_growth_fwd":0.2707,"eps_growth_next":0.1945,"div_yield":0.0012,"roe":0.2332,"roa":0.08596,"de":48.25,"gross_margin":0.5932,"op_margin":0.2152,"profit_margin":0.1856,"current_ratio":1.518},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":22.68,"sector":17.74,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":38.34,"sector":28.93,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":14.46,"sector":5.856,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":74.4